# Phase 339 (STORD-02) — sudoers grant for the whole-disk LUKS2 encryption wrapper.
# Security model: grant on ONE explicit binary path, NO glob, NO arg wildcard.
# The wrapper validates its action enum {format|open|close|status}, re-validates
# every target device root-side against THREE gates (device-shape regex + OS/boot/EFI
# refusal + USB/removable refusal) BEFORE any cryptsetup/mkfs/mount runs, and takes
# the passphrase + recovery key on STDIN only (never argv) — so no caller string can
# format the OS disk, a USB/removable device, or leak a secret via /proc/<pid>/cmdline.
# Deploy: update.sh Step 7.10y (content-diff + subject-template + visudo validate-or-remove).
Cmnd_Alias LIVINITYD_LUKS = /usr/local/lib/livos/livos-luks.sh
bruce ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: LIVINITYD_LUKS
